# Expenses core: /v1/expenses (minus the spreadsheet/receipt imports),
# /v1/budget/snapshots, /v1/budget/items, /v1/reports/{expenses,suggestions}.
# Load parity/expenses-core-setup.sql first, then:
#   go run ./cmd/parity -a http://127.0.0.1:8081 -b http://127.0.0.1:18116 -jwt-secret parity-secret \
#     -cases parity/expenses-core.jsonl -ignore requestId,id,createdAt,updatedAt,generatedAt,revision
# revision is ignored: each mutating case runs on Vapor first, so v2's
# write lands one revision later on the same row.
# Known diff: reports-suggestions and suggestions-after-dismiss format
# amounts with NumberFormatter in Locale.current. A Vapor run on a Mac
# with a pt_PT locale says "1 750,00"/"70,3%"; v2 assumes the en
# formatting ("1,750.00"/"70.3%") of the Linux image. Everything else in
# those two cases matches.
# /v1/reports/overview is not here: v2 leaves it on Vapor until an
# OverviewSource (statistics) is wired.
